WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.301 line:92%
-I want to talk about the movie.

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-But I also --

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got to travel
a little this summer.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.405
-Yeah.
-You went to Amsterdam, which --

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:06.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you have a history
with Amsterdam.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:07.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I lived there
for a couple years.

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:09.109
One of the most beautiful cities
in the world.

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:11.711
-It's the most beautiful -
the most beautiful scenery

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:13.146 line:92%
the most beautiful prostitutes

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:14.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-I wasn't even on drugs.

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:15.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-I didn't do drugs.

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was working.
And also, drugs are bad.

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:21.654 size:78% position:39%
And I was blown away
by how pretty it was.

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:23.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I did go
to the red light district

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:25.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
just to kind of see
and whatever.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
very beautiful ladies.

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:30.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there were -- There were
like, two petite ladies.

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"You guys are doing it!"

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:34.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Doing it for the sisters!

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
Love it.
-Very -- Very hard to find

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:38.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
a petite woman in general
in Amsterdam.

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:40.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
Very tall people, the Dutch.
-Yeah.

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:42.042 line:92%
No, that's why I didn't stay

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:44.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, I just thought
it was so gorgeous.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.179 size:81% position:41%
-You liked the canals?
-I went on the canals.

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:49.649
Like, I ended up -- I ended up
like, you know, just for fun

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:52.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, videoing the whole,
like, canals

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:56.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the scenery and stuff,
as I am wont to.

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:57.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was just sort of, like,
sarcastically

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:59.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
going like, "Ugh, God,
it's ugly here."

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:02.128
Like, "How do you people
even wake up in the mornin

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:03.129 line:92%
and look at the scenery?"

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:03.997 line:92%
And most people understood

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:06.666 size:84% position:42%
that that was me saying
it was very beautiful.

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:09.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there were couple
of Dutch people

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:11.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
who thought I was
being very rude,

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I should go back
to my country.

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:16.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then a fair amount of Dutc
people came to my defense.

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:19.412 size:75% position:38%
So -- But it was all
happening in Dutch.

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:23.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
So now I know
the Dutch word for sarcastic

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.684 size:78% position:39% line:92%
which is sarcastisch.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-So not that hard.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:27.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not that hard.
-So they were going, like,

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:29.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
"She's being sarcastic."
And several said,

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:32.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, "She's just drunk.
So, I also know --

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
Dronken is the Dutch word
for drunk.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:35.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Dronken, yeah.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:39.265
-Yes, I've been dronken
a few times in Amsterdam.

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:40.533 size:88% position:44%
You also -- Did you go
anywhere else in Europe?

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:45.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did. I went to Switzerland,
which is, like, the cute--

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:46.005 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-It's really amazing.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The cutest country.
-Yeah.

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:49.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, I feel --
Like, I'm being patronizing.

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:50.810 line:92%
But I'm sorry, it's so cute.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.213
-Yeah. It makes Amsterdam
look like a garbage can.

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:56.015 line:92%
-Exactly. Like, every hillside

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:58.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
was, like, the most perfectl
designed,

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:00.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, the cutest,
most amazing --

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:01.654 line:92%
And I took a friend of mine.

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:04.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she, you know,
was, like, very grateful

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:04.958 line:92%
to be taken to Switzerland

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:07.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
But as we would crest
every hill,

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:10.330
what am I, an animal? I'm no
going to sing "Sound of Music"

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Of course, yeah.
-I mean --

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:13.333 line:92%
So it was, like, really watching

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:17.170
a test of our friendship,
like, play out on her face

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:20.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
knowing, like, "She bought m
this trip to Switzerland.

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
Be nice."
But then how many times

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:23.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
can I sing, "High on a hil
was a lonely goatherd"

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:26.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
before she murders me
on this hilltop

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:27.480 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and leaves the body?

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It required patience
on her part.

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:30.150 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yes, God bless her.

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:33.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This film is -- It's a little
tricky to describe.

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:36.289
But we were saying backstage
the director, the writer is --

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:38.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. He's like
a British comedy legend.

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, Chris Morris, and -
-Yeah, Chris Morris.

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:42.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, it's --
It is hard to describe.

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:46.733
It's like a dark satire abou
the criminal justice system.

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:50.503 size:81% position:41%
And it really devolves
into, like, a farce,

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:53.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, a full Shakespearean
comedy of errors

00:02:53.173 --> 00:02:55.775
where, like, everybody's
misunderstanding everybody

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:58.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's a really serious
subject matter

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.112 line:92%
because it's about the way

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:01.781 size:84% position:42%
that law enforcement
kind of uses entrapment

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:04.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
and kind of disproportionately
targets minorities.

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:09.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's so funny, which is no
because we take it lightly

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:12.659
but because Chris Morris
is so good at using satire

00:03:12.659 --> 00:03:15.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
to kind of talk
about these subjects.

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:17.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
So a lot of the details
in our movie

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
are, like, trying
to be as absurd

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:22.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
as, like, hundreds
of these true cases.

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because you're basically
an FBI agent

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:25.004 line:92%
who's trying to set somebody u

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
so you can get the credit
for taking them down.

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:30.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly. Like, you know,
everybody's motivated by ego

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:33.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, like, I think
that some people

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.114 line:92%
spend their life thinking

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:38.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
that law enforcement has
our best interests at heart!

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:39.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You know.

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's really
interesting to --

00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:43.790
-I thought you were saying
we were motivated by ego,

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.358 line:92%
which I was also down with

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:48.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was also going to be onboard
with you, there.

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:49.162 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:50.863 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yeah. Both true things.

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:54.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know you shot that
in the Dominican Republic.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now you're shooting
in New York, yes?

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
What's it like
shooting in New York?

00:03:57.337 --> 00:04:00.006
-New York has been great.
Like, I can't believe --

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:02.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel very grown-up
shooting stuff in New York

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:07.146
But I will say, like, when you
shoot in a small town, like,

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:10.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
people are like, "Oh,
I just can't go to work toda

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:12.785
or get into my home becaus
they're filming a movie."

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:13.853 line:92%
Like, "Yeah, whatever you need."

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:16.356
And in New York, they're like,
"I've lived here for 30 years.

00:04:16.356 --> 00:04:19.959
Get the [bleep] off my street.
I'm going to do what I -- No."

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:22.462 size:75% position:38%
And we were shooting
on St. Mark's Place

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:23.763 size:88% position:44% line:92%
at midnight on a Friday.

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:26.266 size:75% position:38%
And nobody was going
to be quiet for us.

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:27.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, like, you know,
there's just guys

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
walking through the shots.
And at one point,

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:33.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
a guy was walking through
the shot and vomited.

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:33.673 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:36.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
And -- And when
something like that happens,

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:39.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
you realize that there's
no, like, department

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:40.680 size:84% position:42% line:92%
for that on a film set.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:44.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's no one whose job it is
to clean up the vomit.

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:47.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was right next to
the director's, like, monitor,

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:50.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
where he's going, like,
"And cut.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:51.758 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Um, some notes?"

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:53.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
But -- So they didn't
have a solution.

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:57.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they just set up little
orange cones around the vomit.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:58.364 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:00.166 size:88% position:44%
But what was crazy is,
I was thinking about it,

00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:02.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was like --
It was little orange cones

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:04.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
which to me suggests
that this happens enough

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:09.108
that they have special orang
cones for vomit situations

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:09.742 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in New York.

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They have, like,
ones for traffic.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then they have
little ones --

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:14.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're, like, just for vomit
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's always so wonderful
to see you here.

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:18.851 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Congrats on the movie.

